-- title:
--   The scalar allowance for a later odd divisor block
-- statement:
--   Let $x\ge1$, $q\ge4$, $(a,q)=1$, $2\gamma=a/q+\beta$, and $|\beta|\le q^{-2}$. On the specified later odd divisor block indexed by $k\in\mathbb N$, the capped Type I envelope sums to at most
--   $$\frac{x\log x}{2q(k+5/4)}+B(x)C(q),$$
--   where $B(x)$ is the ordinary reciprocal budget and $C(q)$ is the defined odd-grid block constant. This is the allowance used when summing all later blocks.
-- source:
--   Terence Tao, Every odd number greater than 1 is the sum of at most five primes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6656, Sections 5 and 6. Original Lean source: Theorems/Thm_TaoFivePrimes_vaughan_typeI_ordinary_block_wrappers.lean, lines 80-200.

